<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2365] Cache inconsistency: concurrent preloading from a storage when OFF HEAP is used</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2365</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Start two server nodes in parallel using &lt;tt&gt;TwoNodesEviction&lt;/tt&gt; example attached.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Both nodes start preloading the full set of data from an underlying storage considering that in a cache only data for which a node is primary will reside.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However the node that joins the topology later will have much more entries in the on-heap part of the cache than expected ignoring eviction policy settings.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If to disable the eviction policy and off-heap then the example works fine.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
